WEBVTT

00:13.687 --> 00:15.272
‎I'm Akine Atagawa.

00:16.481 --> 00:17.524
‎I look forward to...

00:18.900 --> 00:20.694
‎getting to know you.

00:21.945 --> 00:22.946
<i>‎Younger sister...</i>

00:24.072 --> 00:25.699
<i>‎She's Manatsu Atagawa's younger sister?</i>

01:57.541 --> 02:01.962
‎EPISODE 11
‎INVERSION

02:02.671 --> 02:04.256
‎I'm Manatsu Atagawa.

02:04.339 --> 02:05.674
‎I used to play youth basketball.

02:06.174 --> 02:07.676
‎Nice to meet you.

02:08.552 --> 02:09.886
‎Nice to meet you.

02:11.304 --> 02:12.931
<i>‎Back in my first year of middle school,</i>

02:13.014 --> 02:17.769
<i>‎I joined the basketball team
‎after my neighbor, Sacchan, invited me.</i>

02:17.853 --> 02:19.187
‎Koyuki!

02:19.271 --> 02:20.939
‎Thanks for coming.

02:21.439 --> 02:23.066
‎Sorry I'm not Miki.

02:23.150 --> 02:26.653
‎-I'm just happy to have you.
‎-Attack!

02:26.736 --> 02:28.113
‎MIKI JOINED THE VOLLEYBALL TEAM

02:28.196 --> 02:29.197
‎Is she a friend, Sachi?

02:29.281 --> 02:30.657
‎Glad to have you on the team.

02:30.740 --> 02:31.950
‎I'll do my best.

02:32.033 --> 02:34.077
‎-Let's do this!
‎-We'll make a great team!

02:34.161 --> 02:36.204
<i>‎My seniors were kind.</i>

02:36.288 --> 02:37.205
‎GRADE 3 CLASS 1

02:37.289 --> 02:38.373
‎Here.

02:38.456 --> 02:40.792
‎The second and third years
‎will be on the court today.

02:40.876 --> 02:43.128
‎This is a set menu
‎for the first years to practice.

02:43.211 --> 02:44.212
‎Okay.

02:44.921 --> 02:47.674
<i>‎I was glad to have someone I knew.</i>

02:47.757 --> 02:49.176
‎Thanks!

02:51.928 --> 02:53.221
‎Koyuki.

02:53.305 --> 02:54.931
‎Come back soon, 'kay?

02:56.057 --> 02:57.058
‎BOW

02:57.142 --> 02:58.143
‎Such a cutie.

02:58.226 --> 02:59.227
‎Stop bothering her!

02:59.311 --> 03:01.354
<i>‎Which is why I didn't notice it sooner.</i>

03:01.438 --> 03:03.231
‎-Don't do that.
‎-Why not?

03:03.315 --> 03:05.025
‎She didn't like it.

03:05.108 --> 03:06.318
‎What was that?

03:06.818 --> 03:08.236
‎GIRLS BASKETBALL CLUB

03:08.320 --> 03:10.447
‎Only the first years
‎are practicing outside today.

03:10.530 --> 03:13.199
‎The captain gave me a set menu
‎that we can practice from.

03:13.283 --> 03:14.284
‎Hey.

03:15.535 --> 03:17.454
‎Who died and put you in charge?

03:19.539 --> 03:23.543
<i>‎At first, I thought she just
‎didn't like being told what to do.</i>

03:24.836 --> 03:25.962
<i>‎But then...</i>

03:26.046 --> 03:27.756
‎How are we gonna get you taller?

03:27.839 --> 03:28.840
‎CHATTER - STRETCH

03:28.924 --> 03:30.884
‎-Isn't that stretching her neck?
‎-What to do.

03:30.967 --> 03:33.595
<i>‎Then I realized her hostility toward me</i>

03:33.678 --> 03:35.722
<i>‎was because of my affinity
‎with the seniors.</i>

03:38.308 --> 03:42.729
<i>‎Manatsu must think it's weird
‎that I'm so close with Sacchan.</i>

03:42.812 --> 03:44.147
‎CHILDHOOD FRIENDS - CLOSE FRIENDS

03:44.231 --> 03:46.233
‎HOSTILE
‎"I'M BETTER THAN HER"

03:48.235 --> 03:49.236
‎Manatsu.

03:49.903 --> 03:53.823
‎The captain wants to see me during lunch.
‎Would you mind coming with me?

03:56.952 --> 03:58.203
‎Thanks for coming.

03:58.286 --> 04:01.539
‎I don't always feel comfortable going
‎to the third-year classroom on my own.

04:03.541 --> 04:06.461
‎Why does the captain
‎always want to talk to you?

04:06.544 --> 04:08.421
‎I'm just easy to talk to for her, is all.

04:08.505 --> 04:12.217
‎We live nearby, and we've never had any
‎of those regular formalities to limit us.

04:12.926 --> 04:16.346
‎I think you're the one she's got
‎her hopes set on for the team, Manatsu.

04:17.555 --> 04:18.556
‎You think?

04:19.182 --> 04:20.600
‎GRADE 3 CLASS 1

04:21.184 --> 04:23.311
‎Manatsu today as well? Thanks for coming.

04:24.854 --> 04:26.231
‎Are you Koyuki's friend?

04:26.314 --> 04:27.524
‎Don't talk to them. Go away.

04:28.733 --> 04:30.068
‎Yes. My name is Manatsu.

04:30.777 --> 04:32.028
<i>‎So we're friends now?</i>

04:33.113 --> 04:34.281
‎You know what?

04:34.364 --> 04:36.574
‎You're a really great friend.

04:36.658 --> 04:38.285
‎I had you all wrong.

04:38.368 --> 04:39.369
‎Oh, yeah?

04:39.452 --> 04:40.453
‎THANKS, BUT...

04:40.537 --> 04:41.788
<i>‎How did you get to that conclusion?</i>

04:41.871 --> 04:44.416
‎So just "Manatsu" from now on.
‎No more honorifics.

04:45.542 --> 04:49.129
<i>‎Being on Manatsu's good side
‎definitely made club activities easier.</i>

04:49.212 --> 04:50.213
‎Keep your chin up!

04:50.297 --> 04:51.298
‎UM...

04:51.381 --> 04:54.884
<i>‎Manatsu got her chance to talk with the
‎seniors whenever she was with me.</i>

04:54.968 --> 04:57.012
‎-What did you have for lunch?
‎-Hello!

04:57.095 --> 05:00.974
<i>‎We weren't friends based on mutual trust.
‎I was just convenient.</i>

05:02.142 --> 05:05.729
<i>‎So there wasn't any one particular event
‎that caused our friendship to break down.</i>

05:05.812 --> 05:06.813
‎GIRLS BASKETBALL CLUB

05:07.397 --> 05:10.400
‎So of the people in our grade,
‎Hotani and Igarashi are pretty hot, hey?

05:10.483 --> 05:11.568
‎Definitely.

05:11.651 --> 05:12.652
‎KOYUKI'S IMAGE

05:12.736 --> 05:13.820
‎IGARASHI
‎BOTHERS ME FOR NO REASON

05:13.903 --> 05:15.071
‎HOTANI
‎IGARASHI'S RIGHT-HAND MAN

05:15.155 --> 05:16.948
‎And what's your type, Koyuki?

05:17.032 --> 05:19.409
‎I can't even imagine what yours could be.

05:21.202 --> 05:23.413
‎Maybe someone
‎who doesn't make fun of others?

05:23.496 --> 05:26.666
‎We're talking about looks here.
‎Weren't you listening?

05:27.709 --> 05:28.710
‎Oh, right.

05:30.712 --> 05:32.047
‎I have no idea.

05:32.130 --> 05:33.423
‎Okay...

05:33.506 --> 05:36.384
‎AWKWARD SILENCE

05:36.885 --> 05:38.053
‎I'll see you later.

05:38.136 --> 05:39.429
‎-See you.
‎-Bye.

05:43.308 --> 05:45.185
‎That Koyuki girl...

05:45.935 --> 05:47.937
‎She's kind of different, isn't she?

05:48.021 --> 05:50.982
‎Yeah, I feel you.
‎She's kind of gloomy, right?

05:51.066 --> 05:52.067
‎That's it!

05:52.150 --> 05:55.820
‎And I got really annoyed at how slow
‎she was to talk just now. Did you notice?

05:55.904 --> 05:58.323
‎-Like, gimme an answer, girl!
‎-Yes!

05:58.406 --> 06:01.701
<i>‎Our friendship
‎had always been a house of cards.</i>

06:02.285 --> 06:04.370
‎You're a really great friend.

06:05.288 --> 06:07.707
<i>‎She didn't mean for my personality.</i>

06:08.583 --> 06:11.002
<i>‎She meant that I was convenient.</i>

06:12.837 --> 06:14.214
‎You sure do love your grunt work.

06:14.798 --> 06:17.342
‎Surely you have other things to do?

06:18.927 --> 06:20.470
‎She's eating on her own.

06:20.553 --> 06:23.723
‎Her water bottle is so lame.
‎Like, it literally makes me laugh.

06:24.724 --> 06:28.728
<i>‎So it didn't take long
‎for me to be branded as the bad guy.</i>

06:31.314 --> 06:33.942
<i>‎I can't take this anymore.
‎I'm going to quit.</i>

06:35.068 --> 06:38.655
<i>‎I should have just quit
‎and cut all ties with her right away.</i>

06:38.738 --> 06:39.739
‎CLUB WITHDRAWAL FORM

06:40.615 --> 06:41.741
‎You know what?

06:42.408 --> 06:45.495
‎Atagawa's been really
‎coming on strong with me lately.

06:47.080 --> 06:50.583
‎I'm not interested in anyone
‎other than the person I like.

06:51.084 --> 06:52.252
‎It's getting annoying.

06:54.337 --> 06:56.840
<i>‎Manatsu likes Igarashi?</i>

06:59.134 --> 07:00.635
‎Do you understand what I'm saying?

07:04.347 --> 07:06.307
‎Please go out with me, Koyuki.

07:07.350 --> 07:10.270
<i>‎Honestly,
‎the first thing that came to mind was,</i>

07:10.937 --> 07:12.772
<i>‎"He finally said it."</i>

07:13.481 --> 07:16.025
<i>‎And, "Please let go of my hand."</i>

07:16.109 --> 07:17.110
‎STARE

07:17.193 --> 07:20.280
<i>‎And, "He's acting like rejection
‎isn't even in the cards for him."</i>

07:20.989 --> 07:25.535
<i>‎-And, "Why does he even like me?"</i>
‎-Koyuki.

07:25.618 --> 07:27.162
‎-<i>‎All these thoughts...</i>
‎-Koyuki.

07:28.997 --> 07:33.001
<i>‎I felt I needed something more
‎than simply cutting ties.</i>

07:34.210 --> 07:35.211
<i>‎Which is why...</i>

07:35.295 --> 07:36.296
‎Okay.

07:36.796 --> 07:40.592
<i>‎I felt my body, my heart,
‎screaming at me to stop...</i>

07:41.551 --> 07:43.052
‎I'll go out with you.

07:43.136 --> 07:46.347
<i>‎I just pretended I didn't hear it.</i>

07:47.515 --> 07:48.683
<i>‎Not again.</i>

07:49.517 --> 07:52.228
<i>‎I quit the club
‎and started dating Igarashi,</i>

07:52.312 --> 07:55.440
<i>‎and from then on,
‎nothing ever happened directly,</i>

07:55.523 --> 07:57.775
<i>‎but the indirect harassment increased.</i>

07:58.485 --> 08:02.238
<i>‎Probably because she didn't want Igarashi
‎or the boys to know what she was doing.</i>

08:03.281 --> 08:06.784
<i>‎I needed something to prove
‎Manatsu was the one behind it all.</i>

08:06.868 --> 08:08.203
‎Morning, Koyun.

08:08.786 --> 08:11.789
‎For once, I got here with time to spare...

08:12.290 --> 08:13.291
‎What...

08:16.544 --> 08:18.963
‎Atagawa...

08:19.047 --> 08:20.256
‎Let go of me!

08:27.472 --> 08:28.473
‎The glass!

08:28.556 --> 08:31.017
‎Miki, you're bleeding!
‎We gotta get you cleaned up.

08:31.100 --> 08:32.560
‎No, wait!

08:32.644 --> 08:34.020
‎What? Blood?

08:34.103 --> 08:35.104
‎Was there a fight?

08:40.193 --> 08:41.528
‎Well, look at you.

08:41.611 --> 08:44.489
‎Hiding first behind the boys,
‎and now Miki?

08:44.572 --> 08:48.993
‎You go around with this "poor me" act
‎and you literally leech off others.

08:49.077 --> 08:50.370
‎Aren't you ashamed?

08:51.829 --> 08:52.872
‎Not really.

08:53.498 --> 08:56.292
‎At least I don't go around
‎harassing people in childish ways.

08:56.376 --> 08:57.961
‎I'd be more ashamed of that.

08:59.045 --> 09:01.256
‎I told you. That wasn't me.

09:01.339 --> 09:03.258
‎Who else would do it but you?

09:03.341 --> 09:05.009
‎How should I know?

09:05.093 --> 09:07.136
‎Plenty of people
‎pass by those shoe lockers.

09:07.220 --> 09:08.304
‎Are you really that stupid?

09:10.682 --> 09:12.392
‎-I never mentioned that.
‎-What?

09:12.475 --> 09:16.646
‎Nobody ever said anything
‎about this being in my shoe locker.

09:17.730 --> 09:19.148
‎Hey, over here!

09:19.732 --> 09:21.359
‎Here! Over here!

09:22.777 --> 09:24.654
‎You dug your own grave, Manatsu.

09:24.737 --> 09:25.905
<i>‎Come on.</i>

09:25.989 --> 09:27.407
‎Are you really that stupid?

09:27.490 --> 09:28.533
<i>‎Come on!</i>

09:29.617 --> 09:30.952
‎Listen, you!

09:31.035 --> 09:34.622
‎You've got some nerve ditching the club
‎to start your own little clique.

09:34.706 --> 09:37.875
‎We all know deep down you're just a gloomy
‎loner who can't do anything on her own.

09:38.585 --> 09:39.627
<i>‎Stay like that.</i>

09:39.711 --> 09:40.878
‎What are you smiling at?

09:40.962 --> 09:42.213
‎What are you doing?

09:43.506 --> 09:44.507
‎Igarashi?

09:44.591 --> 09:47.635
‎Hey, hey, hey...

09:48.678 --> 09:51.389
‎The hell is this?
‎What are you doing to her, Atagawa?

09:52.265 --> 09:53.600
‎Are you all right, Koyuki?

09:56.102 --> 09:57.395
‎That hurt.

10:02.233 --> 10:03.901
‎Way to go, Igarashi!

10:05.153 --> 10:06.321
‎You da prince!

10:07.238 --> 10:09.449
‎How lovely for you, Koyuki.

10:09.532 --> 10:12.577
‎Such sweet crocodile tears.
‎You're such a girlie girl.

10:12.660 --> 10:13.661
‎So very "cute."

10:14.829 --> 10:17.415
‎You play the victim
‎for your knight in shining armor.

10:17.498 --> 10:19.167
‎You're such a poser.

10:20.460 --> 10:23.463
‎Hey! What did you just hiss at her?

10:24.422 --> 10:25.798
‎Let's go, Koyuki.

10:28.968 --> 10:30.386
<i>‎Manatsu Atagawa.</i>

10:31.888 --> 10:33.806
<i>‎Akine is her younger sister.</i>

10:34.682 --> 10:37.810
<i>‎Just how much does she know about me?</i>

10:39.896 --> 10:40.897
‎FLUFFY FLUFFY

10:40.980 --> 10:42.231
<i>‎I really hate this!</i>

10:42.315 --> 10:45.818
<i>‎The more I think about it,
‎the more I hate middle school.</i>

10:45.902 --> 10:49.989
<i>‎No, more than that...
‎I hate who I was back then.</i>

10:54.911 --> 10:57.580
‎You're on social media now?

10:57.664 --> 11:00.333
‎Yeah, I just started
‎thanks to Miharu and Sora.

11:00.416 --> 11:02.752
‎MIHARU - SORA
‎FRIENDS FROM MIDDLE SCHOOL

11:02.835 --> 11:03.920
‎Found one.

11:04.003 --> 11:06.089
‎So this is Manatsu's sister?

11:06.172 --> 11:07.507
‎#SISTERS #BESTIES

11:07.590 --> 11:08.591
‎Besties?

11:10.218 --> 11:13.262
‎What's this?
‎Koyun and Miki. What are you up to?

11:14.681 --> 11:16.349
‎What? Atagawa?

11:17.016 --> 11:19.352
‎We're in the same class.
‎We chat all the time.

11:19.936 --> 11:23.689
‎Akine says you've told her
‎some things about me.

11:24.482 --> 11:26.609
‎What exactly have you told her?

11:26.692 --> 11:29.862
‎Just that we've been friends
‎for, like, forever?

11:30.488 --> 11:33.991
‎Koyun! If you and I get married,
‎you and Miki will be related. Cool, right?

11:34.075 --> 11:35.243
‎That's brilliant!

11:35.326 --> 11:36.702
‎Sure. Whatever.

11:36.786 --> 11:39.956
‎I said we might even
‎get married in the future.

11:40.456 --> 11:41.791
‎Why would you say that?

11:42.291 --> 11:44.710
‎Well, in the end...

11:44.794 --> 11:45.795
‎BAHA!

11:45.878 --> 11:48.631
‎...I have zero clue
‎as to what's going on in her mind.

11:48.714 --> 11:50.466
‎Atagawa's the "cool girl" type, after all.

11:51.134 --> 11:52.135
‎BWAHAHA

11:52.218 --> 11:54.470
‎She's not a bad person. Probably? Maybe?

11:55.304 --> 11:57.473
<i>‎Or so Yuki says...</i>

11:57.557 --> 12:01.227
<i>‎I have no idea
‎how much she knows about me.</i>

12:01.811 --> 12:05.481
<i>‎She could know parts of me
‎that I don't want anyone to know.</i>

12:05.565 --> 12:06.816
‎VARIOUS MEMORIES

12:06.899 --> 12:09.235
<i>‎That alone makes me feel very uneasy.</i>

12:10.069 --> 12:14.240
<i>‎Please... Please don't let us
‎have to interact much going forward...</i>

12:32.508 --> 12:34.051
<i>‎Of course.</i>

12:34.135 --> 12:36.929
<i>‎We live in the same neighborhood.
‎Of course our school routes overlap.</i>

12:38.139 --> 12:42.935
‎Are the first years not doing
‎morning practice for soccer yet?

12:43.519 --> 12:45.354
‎There's no morning practice today.

12:46.731 --> 12:47.773
‎Okay...

12:48.774 --> 12:50.318
‎DEAD SILENT

12:50.401 --> 12:51.694
<i>‎This is awkward.</i>

12:52.278 --> 12:55.990
<i>‎At times like these, it's the older person
‎who should initiate conversation, right?</i>

12:56.616 --> 12:58.493
<i>‎But what do we even talk about?</i>

12:59.869 --> 13:02.747
<i>‎What do we have in common?
‎I don't want to talk about middle school.</i>

13:02.830 --> 13:04.832
‎COMMONALITIES
‎TALK ABOUT MIDDLE SCHOOL

13:04.916 --> 13:05.917
‎HIGH SCHOOL LIFE

13:06.000 --> 13:08.211
<i>‎High school life?
‎Would that even be stimulating?</i>

13:09.587 --> 13:11.631
<i>‎What do I do?
‎I'm so bad at making conversation.</i>

13:11.714 --> 13:12.715
‎TOO LATE

13:16.302 --> 13:17.428
‎Morning.

13:18.763 --> 13:19.764
‎PHEW

13:19.847 --> 13:20.848
‎Amamiya.

13:21.849 --> 13:22.850
‎WHOA

13:22.934 --> 13:23.935
‎THUMP THUMP THUMP

13:24.018 --> 13:25.853
<i>‎Why did she react like that?</i>

13:25.937 --> 13:27.230
<i>‎What a relief.</i>

13:27.313 --> 13:28.689
<i>‎Now I'm saved.</i>

13:28.773 --> 13:30.858
‎Good morning, Amamiya.

13:31.442 --> 13:32.944
‎Are you two walking together?

13:33.444 --> 13:34.695
‎We just met on the train.

13:35.196 --> 13:38.115
‎MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

13:38.199 --> 13:40.243
‎So you like that song too?

13:40.326 --> 13:41.827
‎I listen to it all the time.

13:42.411 --> 13:45.873
<i>‎Wow. He's doing a great job
‎keeping our conversation flowing.</i>

13:46.624 --> 13:51.337
<i>‎I'm sorry, Amamiya, for thinking
‎your questions were tiring back then.</i>

13:52.004 --> 13:54.924
<i>‎And I'm also sorry for laughing at you
‎when you were flustered.</i>

13:55.466 --> 13:56.842
‎STARE

13:57.343 --> 13:59.220
‎What? Is there something on me?

13:59.720 --> 14:00.721
‎PFT PFT

14:00.805 --> 14:05.810
‎No, I was just thinking I feel bad for
‎teasing you that time over spring break.

14:05.893 --> 14:07.395
‎You only feel that now?

14:07.478 --> 14:11.190
‎Hey, do you think you'd forget about that
‎if I push the pressure point on your head?

14:11.274 --> 14:12.858
‎There's a pressure point that does that?

14:12.942 --> 14:14.235
‎-It's around here.
‎-I block.

14:14.318 --> 14:15.319
‎CHATTER CHATTER

14:15.403 --> 14:17.280
‎Let me find a work-around. Here...

14:17.780 --> 14:19.156
‎You're good friends, hey?

14:19.240 --> 14:23.703
‎Not at all. She's a bully.
‎She's got dirt on me.

14:23.786 --> 14:25.162
‎Hey, no...

14:31.252 --> 14:32.962
‎Good morning, Akine.

14:33.462 --> 14:34.505
‎Momoka.

14:34.589 --> 14:37.174
‎I saw you, so I came running.

14:37.258 --> 14:39.677
<i>‎Wow, she looks just like a doll.</i>

14:40.261 --> 14:42.930
‎And Amamiya. Good morning to you too.

14:43.806 --> 14:47.435
‎Kuriki, right? I remember you
‎from when you came to check out our club.

14:47.518 --> 14:49.812
‎You remember me?

14:50.354 --> 14:55.192
‎I decided not to join after all,
‎so I haven't been back.

14:55.776 --> 14:57.653
‎That's fine. Don't worry about that.

14:57.737 --> 14:59.447
‎Atagawa's joined, after all.

14:59.530 --> 15:01.240
‎But I...

15:01.324 --> 15:03.576
‎I think you'll do great, Akine.

15:04.076 --> 15:05.369
<i>‎She's luminous.</i>

15:06.287 --> 15:07.455
‎SNAP

15:09.916 --> 15:11.709
<i>‎I know this feeling.</i>

15:11.792 --> 15:14.587
<i>‎I don't think I'm welcome here.</i>

15:15.296 --> 15:17.548
<i>‎I'll just leave for class then.</i>

15:21.427 --> 15:22.595
<i>‎What?</i>

15:25.681 --> 15:28.100
‎Well then, Amamiya. See you later.

15:28.684 --> 15:30.102
‎See you at cheer training.

15:34.774 --> 15:35.775
‎Why'd you do that?

15:35.858 --> 15:40.029
‎I figured you were going
‎to just float off again.

15:41.864 --> 15:42.865
‎HEH

15:42.949 --> 15:44.909
‎-You got me.
‎-You're very obvious.

15:47.244 --> 15:48.245
‎WHOOSH WHOOSH

15:48.329 --> 15:51.207
‎You know, I kind of feel like a dog
‎being taken for walkies.

15:51.290 --> 15:52.541
‎Shall we go for run by the river?

15:52.625 --> 15:54.251
‎PONTA

15:54.335 --> 15:55.419
‎No running.

15:56.963 --> 16:00.925
‎I didn't think Amamiya would remember me.

16:01.509 --> 16:04.512
‎Because you only went once, right?

16:04.595 --> 16:06.514
‎I went twice.

16:07.264 --> 16:08.265
‎All right.

16:09.141 --> 16:10.768
‎Hey, Akine.

16:11.268 --> 16:14.689
‎Do you think Amamiya has a girlfriend?

16:16.148 --> 16:18.150
‎CHATTER CHATTER

16:18.734 --> 16:20.152
‎Who knows?

16:21.028 --> 16:22.405
‎Could you find out for me?

16:26.659 --> 16:29.161
‎Enjoying your new class?

16:31.747 --> 16:35.292
‎I don't like the way
‎you keep grinning at me.

16:35.376 --> 16:37.169
‎IRREGULAR CATCH UP OVER A MEAL

16:37.753 --> 16:40.798
‎When you're happy, Yota, I'm happy.

16:41.298 --> 16:43.676
‎Now you look like a Buddha statue.

16:45.469 --> 16:48.180
‎I didn't realize I was such a sticky beak.

16:48.973 --> 16:51.017
‎I could ask the same. How about you?

16:51.100 --> 16:53.310
‎What? No. Never.

16:53.394 --> 16:54.395
‎HMPH

16:54.478 --> 16:56.188
‎Now you're a wrathful deity...

16:56.272 --> 16:59.108
‎There was one guy in middle school.

16:59.191 --> 17:01.193
‎We dated for a little bit.

17:02.194 --> 17:04.947
<i>‎I tried to get to know him,
‎even if only a little.</i>

17:05.614 --> 17:09.326
<i>‎I went out with him
‎assuming the love would eventually follow.</i>

17:09.910 --> 17:11.579
‎But it didn't go well at all.

17:12.413 --> 17:17.835
‎I realized love
‎isn't something you can force.

17:17.918 --> 17:19.336
‎IMPURE MOTIVES

17:19.420 --> 17:21.839
<i>‎And that wasn't the only reason
‎we started dating...</i>

17:21.922 --> 17:22.923
‎BUT SURELY YOU?

17:23.007 --> 17:25.593
‎-But that's not the case with you, right?
‎-Don't ask me.

17:25.676 --> 17:26.677
‎LOVE

17:26.761 --> 17:29.096
‎Love can come in all shapes and sizes.

17:29.180 --> 17:32.641
<i>‎If two kinds of love don't match,
‎one person is bound to suffer.</i>

17:32.725 --> 17:34.477
‎WHAT? - I LOVE YOU
‎DIFFERENT TYPE

17:34.560 --> 17:36.062
‎LIKE - LOVE
‎DIFFERENT SIZE

17:36.145 --> 17:39.940
<i>‎It's hard, because it's not enough
‎to just be liked, or to just love.</i>

17:40.024 --> 17:41.233
‎I'M THE ONLY ONE IN PAIN

17:41.317 --> 17:43.861
‎I guess love
‎is still a long ways off for me.

17:43.944 --> 17:44.945
‎CREEP CREEP

17:45.029 --> 17:46.238
<i>‎Soot, soot...</i>

17:46.322 --> 17:48.824
‎LIVING IT NOW

17:48.908 --> 17:50.743
‎-That hurts to hear.
‎-<i>‎Soot, soot...</i>

17:51.619 --> 17:53.746
‎-Go away! Get lost!
‎-<i>‎Soot, soot...</i>

17:55.748 --> 17:56.749
‎I'm sorry.

17:56.832 --> 17:57.833
‎GYOZA FESTIVAL
‎EVEN MORE GYOZA

17:57.917 --> 18:00.169
‎-I didn't mean it that way.
‎-I said it's fine.

18:00.252 --> 18:01.670
‎Those were some tasty gyoza.

18:01.754 --> 18:02.755
‎How about gyoza?

18:02.838 --> 18:05.216
‎But then our breath will smell.

18:05.299 --> 18:07.301
<i>‎They're from our school.</i>

18:08.469 --> 18:10.387
‎RUSH RUSH

18:12.473 --> 18:14.892
‎Seniors. How awkward.

18:15.392 --> 18:17.770
‎And on a gyoza date.
‎Kinda low-key cool, hey?

18:17.853 --> 18:19.396
<i>‎That girl just now...</i>

18:23.317 --> 18:25.277
‎Sorry if my breath stinks.

18:25.361 --> 18:27.822
‎Mine stinks too, so I couldn't tell.

18:41.127 --> 18:42.378
‎Good morning.

18:42.962 --> 18:44.672
‎You scared me!

18:44.755 --> 18:47.258
‎You shouldn't walk and read.
‎It's dangerous.

18:47.967 --> 18:48.968
‎CLOSE

18:49.051 --> 18:50.511
‎-Tsk.
‎-Don't "tsk" me.

18:51.095 --> 18:52.388
‎What were you reading?

18:52.471 --> 18:53.806
‎I...

18:53.889 --> 18:55.266
‎THE CURIOUS CASE
‎OF THE PET MANOR

18:55.349 --> 18:56.559
‎What's this? Looks lame.

18:56.642 --> 18:58.394
‎NERVOUS WHEN TALKING ABOUT
‎THE THINGS SHE LIKES WITH OTHERS

18:58.477 --> 18:59.603
‎Hey, I know that one.

19:00.729 --> 19:02.898
‎I haven't read the book,
‎but I've seen the movie.

19:03.399 --> 19:04.400
‎It's a good story, hey?

19:05.025 --> 19:06.402
‎MELTS

19:07.069 --> 19:09.989
‎There's another movie based on a book
‎by the same author airing on TV this week.

19:10.072 --> 19:12.408
‎Yes. I saw that one in theaters.

19:12.992 --> 19:14.994
‎I liked the original,

19:15.077 --> 19:18.164
‎so I was excited to see
‎how they'd adapt it for the screen.

19:18.247 --> 19:20.666
<i>‎Hey, she's in a good mood.</i>

19:21.167 --> 19:23.419
‎Well, if you recommend it,
‎I'll have to give it a watch.

19:25.421 --> 19:26.922
<i>‎She seems happy?</i>

19:29.592 --> 19:31.093
<i>‎She's cute.</i>

19:32.344 --> 19:34.471
‎But sorry in advance
‎if it's not to your liking.

19:34.555 --> 19:36.557
‎EMOTIONS GRAPH
‎I MAY HAVE SET THE BAR TOO HIGH

19:36.640 --> 19:38.517
‎Why so negative? It'll be fine.

19:45.274 --> 19:48.152
‎Amamiya! Good morning.

19:48.235 --> 19:50.487
‎Kuriki. Good morning.

19:50.571 --> 19:53.616
‎Are you going
‎to this morning's cheer practice?

19:53.699 --> 19:55.743
‎No, I have club activities.

19:56.243 --> 19:58.162
‎But you're in the cheer squad.
‎Right, Koyun?

19:58.245 --> 19:59.663
‎Yeah.

20:00.539 --> 20:02.124
<i>‎Koyun?</i>

20:04.376 --> 20:05.377
‎Good morning.

20:06.378 --> 20:07.922
‎THE CONVERSATION DIED

20:10.549 --> 20:11.592
‎Koyun.

20:12.092 --> 20:13.636
<i>‎It sounds so strange.</i>

20:13.719 --> 20:16.931
‎I saw you yesterday, right?
‎Outside the restaurant.

20:17.014 --> 20:18.515
‎Yeah, you did.

20:19.016 --> 20:21.185
<i>‎I didn't think she'd recognize me.</i>

20:21.268 --> 20:25.189
‎That tall guy you were with,
‎was he your boyfriend?

20:26.273 --> 20:28.317
‎No, we're just friends.

20:28.400 --> 20:32.446
‎But you looked so good together.
‎I thought you were a couple.

20:33.364 --> 20:35.532
<i>‎I don't remember much about him though.</i>

20:36.659 --> 20:39.453
<i>‎No way... Is that how people see us?</i>

20:40.037 --> 20:41.747
<i>‎This is a troublesome misunderstanding.</i>

20:41.830 --> 20:43.207
‎Yay!

20:43.290 --> 20:46.627
‎I mean it.
‎It really isn't like that between us.

20:46.710 --> 20:48.462
‎We're really just good friends.

20:48.545 --> 20:51.465
‎That sounds so nice.

20:51.548 --> 20:57.012
‎Then do you and Amamiya ever go out
‎for meals like that? Just the two of you?

20:59.556 --> 21:00.975
‎Just the two of us?

21:01.058 --> 21:02.977
‎-Not really.
‎-No.

21:03.060 --> 21:04.311
‎We could?

21:04.395 --> 21:05.854
‎It's okay. Don't force it.

21:06.939 --> 21:08.482
<i>‎But I'm being serious.</i>

21:12.152 --> 21:15.572
‎I don't want to pry
‎into other people's private lives.

21:15.656 --> 21:16.949
‎You can ask him yourself.

21:17.032 --> 21:19.201
<i>‎You're mean.</i>

21:21.120 --> 21:23.163
‎Is your girlfriend
‎strict about that sort of thing?

21:23.247 --> 21:25.457
‎What? No, I don't even have a girlfriend.

21:25.541 --> 21:26.667
‎Wow, really?

21:26.750 --> 21:29.336
‎But you seem like you'd be
‎super popular with the ladies.

21:29.420 --> 21:31.130
‎Don't you agree, Koyun?

21:31.714 --> 21:32.715
‎-WE BROKE UP.
‎-AGAIN?

21:32.798 --> 21:33.882
‎CONVERSATION FROM A WHILE BACK

21:33.966 --> 21:34.967
‎Yeah, I think so.

21:35.551 --> 21:37.469
‎You do seem to have
‎a lot of dating experience.

21:39.054 --> 21:41.265
‎I do not! Not at all!

21:42.266 --> 21:44.810
‎Methinks the man doth protest too much...

21:46.478 --> 21:47.521
‎You're right.

21:47.604 --> 21:48.731
‎Hey.

21:48.814 --> 21:50.983
‎Hey, wait...

21:51.483 --> 21:53.444
‎Is that really the impression I give?

21:59.241 --> 22:01.869
<i>‎And what would make him protest so much...</i>

23:34.002 --> 23:36.171
‎GRADE 1 CLASS 1

23:39.675 --> 23:40.926
‎Akine.

23:41.009 --> 23:42.010
‎LA-DI-DA

23:42.094 --> 23:43.762
‎Amamiya says he doesn't have a girlfriend.

23:43.846 --> 23:45.681
‎And you came to tell me because?

23:47.683 --> 23:50.519
‎So isn't this your big chance?

23:52.312 --> 23:53.438
‎You're right!

23:53.939 --> 23:55.941
‎Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
